# Quality Gates

- Preserve the repository LF policy. Do not change `core.autocrlf` to solve an individual
  file; inspect `.gitattributes` and the actual diff instead.
- Do not run `spotlessApply` automatically. It formats all configured Java sources and
  can create hundreds of unrelated changes. Use `spotlessCheck` for verification.
- Never stage files automatically. Keep formatting-only changes separate from functional
  changes and inspect `git diff --stat` and `git diff --check`.
- Before handoff, run:
  `gradlew.bat spotlessCheck checkstyleMain checkstyleTest checkstyleRewriteRecipes`
  on Windows, or the equivalent `./gradlew` command elsewhere.
- Run `python scripts/i18n/extract-context.py --check` when Java or translation sources
  change.
- Do not refactor or format `src_v19/`; it is a frozen compatibility reference.
